# Independent scope judge, third pass, reading the plan by path and the staged diff.
# 
# Scope. The staged set is exactly three paths: NOTES.md, public/sw.js and the new
# tools/offline-shell-walk.mjs — Steps 3, 1 and 2. HEAD is claude/promote-024 per
# Step 4, and VERSION is absent from the diff as Step 4 requires. Nothing from
# "Not in this plan" appears: no update-strip code, no export-pool code, no roadmap
# bullet, no decision record, no manifest edit, and .branch-guard is untouched. That
# last is stated positively because it is the shape a walk usually arrives in: this
# one drives a browser, its header says so, and it is correctly not in also=. Its
# claim that walk-all "finds it on disk" is true with no edit, because walk-all globs
# *-walk.mjs rather than carrying a list.
# 
# The cache-first servableCopy is inside Step 1. Step 1's sentence names two call
# sites and this is a third, but Step 2 declares check 1 as "nothing in any cache is
# redirected" — a property quantified over every cache and therefore over every path
# that writes into one, of which sw.js has exactly three. Leaving one uncleaned would
# make the plan's own check pass by coincidence rather than by construction. The
# change adds no behaviour on this deploy and its comment says so rather than claiming
# a fix. Step 1's sentence is under-specified; the diff does not over-reach.
# 
# The five follow-ups from the previous pass are real and complete. The walk count is
# right: 47 files match walk-all's glob with this applied, 46 before. Exactly 12 walks
# contain 8131 and no --port handling. alsoAt is now character-for-character the same
# rule as deployServesAt in the walk, so the walk asserts the worker against the deploy
# rather than against a second copy of the worker's own logic. Every fetch( in src/
# targets examples/*.dng, stickers/manifest.json, an icon PNG or tile.file — none is
# "./" or an index page — so the navigation-branch comment is accurate. macro.html does
# carry id="stage" and the three titles are distinct, so check 3's IR assertion is
# load-bearing.
# 
# Run three times rather than read. Clean: all three green. --plant=redirect: checks 1
# and 3 fail, 14 redirected entries (7 pages under both keys), check 3 as net::ERR_FAILED
# — the browser refusing the redirected response, which is the device's defect.
# --plant=alias: checks 2 and 3 fail, 6 missing, check 3 served /ir titled "Photography
# Studio" — the launcher in place of the editor at the extensionless url, which confirms
# the 308-replay claim and proves the title clause. --plant=nonsense exits 2. Afterwards
# the tree is still the three staged paths, port 8137 does not answer and no browser
# remains. That discharges the plan's verification line.
# 
# Six non-blocking observations recorded for follow-up, none a scope problem: the walk's
# openOffline contract block sits above the IR_TITLE constant rather than the function;
# the new file is mode 100644 where the other walks are 100755; a leftover double blank
# line above ctx.close(); check 2's "exactly the set install put there" is slightly
# stronger than the code supports, since the runtime put paths also write into CACHE
# during online browsing; servableCopy rebuilding with a null-body status would throw on
# an unreachable 204/205/304; and install now writes the "/" key twice concurrently,
# benign but unmentioned. Also noted and deliberately left alone: isNavigation still uses
